acpi: logical comparisons compare strings and buffers as their bytes

LEqual, LLess and the other comparisons took a string's or a buffer's
first 4 bytes as an integer, copying a buffer into a 4-byte array: a
longer buffer (a UUID compared in a ThinkPad T15's devices' _STA and
_INI) panicked with "range end index 16 out of range for slice of
length 4", which stopped the interpreter, and a right operand that was
not a buffer panicked too. They now compare the bytes lexicographically,
the right operand converted to the left's type (the spec's section
19.3.5); LAnd and LOr read their operands as integers.

Derived from acpi, so under acpi's license (MIT or Apache-2.0).

